          "collection_date": "2018-08-01",
          "description": {
            "comment": "The common tern is a Holarctic colonially breeding and long-distance migratory seabird. At one of its populations, located in the Banter See at Wilhelmshaven on the German North Sea coast (53.36N, 8.06S), it has been the subject of an individual-based study since 1992. Here, automated monitoring combined with non-invasive sampling methods allows the life-long and holistic assessment of colony presence, reproductive behaviour and performance, migratory behaviour and survival, as well as genetics and physiology. From this study population (Permit # AZ 3319-42502-04-16/2113, Funding : Max Planck Society, Grant ID : MPRG grant to ML), Sandra Bouwhuis, of the Institute of Avian Research, collected a sample from a female breeder. This sample was used to generate chromosomal level reference assembly as part of the G10K-VGP Project and the B10K Project.",
